*----
*  RBMK-1000 LATTICE CELL  --  A3 rebuild, 2026-09-22
*
*  Replaces rbmk_cell_v3.x2m, which was TCWU07 (a CANDU-6 37-element bundle)
*  with the outer square resized.  That cell had a 3.85 cm solid zirconium
*  "calandria tube" occupying 33% of the lattice, 37 pins instead of 18, and
*  only 45% graphite.  It gave a void coefficient of -183 to -621 pcm/%void.
*
*  GEOMETRY  (all radii in cm; DRAGON GEO: coordinates are centimetres)
*  Built by rbmk_proc/RbmkGeo.c2m since 2026-09-24 (3); this table documents it.
*  ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*   r 0.000 - 0.600  carrier rod, Zr, 12 mm solid       MIX 9   [D p.11]
*   r 0.600 - 0.625  rod <-> central tube annulus       MIX 1   [D p.11]
*   r 0.625 - 0.750  central tube Zr, 15 x 1.25 mm      MIX 9   [D p.11]
*   r 0.000 - 4.000  channel coolant, holds the cluster MIX 1   [D p.54]
*   r 4.000 - 4.400  pressure tube Zr-2.5%Nb, 88x4 mm   MIX 2   [D p.54]
*   r 4.400 - 4.550  gas clearance, ring <-> tube       MIX 3   [CAST]
*   r 4.550 - 5.700  graphite rings (split sleeves)     MIX 4   [D p.11]
*   r 5.700 - corner graphite block, bore 11.4 cm dia   MIX 5   [D p.11]
*   half-pitch 12.5 (250 mm lattice)                            [D p.11]
*
*  FUEL ROD  18 rods, two rings of 6 and 12, around a carrier rod
*   r 0.0000 - 0.1000  central hole (2 mm dia), gas     MIX 3   [RU-A][LEI05][BIB]
*   r 0.1000 - 0.5750  UO2 pellet (11.5 mm dia)         MIX 6/7 [D p.11]
*   r 0.5750 - 0.5850  pellet-clad gap, gas             MIX 3   [D p.11][RU-A]
*   r 0.5850 - 0.6790  clad Zr-1%Nb, 13.58 x ID 11.7    MIX 8   [RU-A][LEI05]
*   inner ring  6 rods at R = 1.60 (circle dia 32)              [RU-A][LEI05]
*   outer ring 12 rods at R = 3.10 (circle dia 62), offset pi/12
*                                                   [RU-A][LEI05], phase [D p.96]
*
*  [D] Dollezhal & Emelyanov, "Kanal'nyy yadernyy energeticheskiy reaktor",
*      Atomizdat, Moscow, 1980.  Page numbers are PDF pages of the scan.
*      Chief designer's own monograph, PRE-dating the 1986 modifications,
*      so it describes the as-built Unit 4 configuration.
*  Other tags are listed with full citations in sources/README.md.
*
*  RESOLVED 2026-09-24 against [D]:
*   1. Pressure tube.  [D p.54], describing fig 3.3: the channel body's middle
*      section is "a tube with OUTER diameter 88 and wall thickness 4 mm, of
*      Zr+2.5% Nb".  Repeated [D p.11]; the 80 mm bore is confirmed twice more
*      elsewhere in the text.  So OD 88 -> r 4.40, ID 80 -> r 4.00, which is
*      what this deck already had.  The Wikipedia "8.4 cm ID" reading (which
*      would imply OD 92) is WRONG.  The 10% coolant-area ambiguity is closed.
*   3. Carrier.  [D p.11]: the 18 rods are held by spacer grids on a CENTRAL
*      TUBE of Zr "of size 15 x 1.25 mm" (OD 15, ID 12.5); inside that tube
*      runs "either a carrier rod of diameter 12 mm, or a carrier tube of size
*      12 x 2.5 mm".  The solid 12 mm rod is the standard channel and is what
*      is modelled here; the 12 x 2.5 tube variant carries the DKE power
*      sensor and is not the average channel.  The previous 13 mm OD tube with
*      coolant inside matched NEITHER component.
*   4. Fuel rod.  [D p.11]: clad 13.5 x 0.9, pellet 11.5 mm, UO2 density up
*      to 10.5 g/cm3, enrichment 1.8 or 2% U-235.  The deck had clad 13.6 with
*      an 0.825 wall (ID 11.95), making the pellet-clad gap ~2.3x too thick.
*
*  RESOLVED 2026-09-24 (3) against sources beyond [D]:
*   4a. Clad OD refined 13.5 -> 13.58.  Every source agrees on ID 11.7, which
*      is what fixes the pellet-clad gap: [D] 13.5 x 0.9, [RU-A] the drawing
*      tolerance "13.58 +0.05/-0.07, ID 11.7 +0.1", [LEI05] 13.6 / ID 11.7.
*      [D]'s 13.5 reads as a rounded nominal.  [TD722] p.107 gives the
*      nominal clad-to-channel-wall gap as "2.2 mm"; this deck gives 2.21,
*      and 2.25 at OD 13.5.  Weaker: [RU-B] gives a "minimum gap between fuel
*      rods 1.7 mm".  The tightest gap in this cell is 1.71 (central tube to
*      inner rod), but its tightest ROD-to-rod gap is 2.42, so that match
*      depends on reading "between rods" loosely.  Not relied on.
*   2. Ring radii 1.60 / 3.10 CONFIRMED.  [RU-A] and [LEI05] both give rod
*      circles of dia 32 mm (6 rods) and dia 62 mm (12 rods).  The [TD722]
*      2.2 mm wall gap above checks the outer radius independently.
*      Fig 5.1 section B-B [D p.96] fixes the phase: inner rods at 0 + 60k deg, outer at 15 + 30k deg, which is
*      APIN pi/12 below.  An earlier reading of that figure put the inner
*      ring at 17-18 mm.  That was WRONG: never measure dimensions off a scan.
*   5. Pellet central hole 2 mm CONFIRMED.  [RU-A] (RBMK-1000) and [LEI05]
*      Table 1 (11.52 mm pellet, 2.0 mm hole).  [BIB] (VNIINM, the fuel
*      designer) lists "fuel pellets with central holes" among the RBMK-1000
*      rod design features.  [D] is silent, not contradicting.  Mass check:
*      [PAV] gives 114.7 kg U per assembly at Unit 4.  This cell over [D p.97]'s
*      6937 mm active length gives 115.3 kg with the hole (+0.5%),
*      118.9 kg solid (+3.7%).
*   6. Graphite gas gap CONFIRMED as an idealisation.  [CAST]: 20 mm split
*      rings, alternately tight on the tube (1.5 mm clearance to the block)
*      and tight on the block (1.3 mm clearance to the tube).  So every height
*      has one ~1.3-1.5 mm gas gap.  The 1.5 mm at the tube modelled here
*      represents it; its radial position is immaterial for a gas.
*
*  CROSS-CHECK ON GRAPHITE  (independent of the geometry above)
*   Bore 11.4 cm in a 25 cm pitch leaves 522.9/625 = 83.7% of the cell as
*   block graphite.  With ~2000 bored columns in a 14 m stack, the stack-average
*   graphite fraction is ~86.8%; at 1.65 g/cm3 that is 1763 t against the
*   published ~1700 t.  Agreement to 4% confirms pitch, bore and density.
*
*  TARGET VOLUME FRACTIONS (asserted at the end of this deck)
*   graphite 89.59%  coolant 3.60%  fuel 2.90%  Zr 3.03%  gas 0.87%
*   Recomputed analytically 2026-09-24 (3) for clad OD 13.58 (was 3.65 / 2.98
*   at OD 13.5; graphite, fuel and gas unchanged by that step).
*   Recomputed analytically 2026-09-24 for the corrected carrier and clad.
*   Change from the pre-correction geometry (which read 3.77 / 2.73 / 1.00):
*     coolant  -3.2% relative   (less water in the channel)
*     Zr       +9.3% relative   (solid 12 mm carrier is much more metal than
*                                the 13 mm hollow tube it replaces)
*     gas     -13.3% relative   (pellet-clad gap was ~2.3x too thick)
*   graphite and fuel are UNCHANGED, so the 1763 t graphite cross-check and
*   the fuel fraction both still hold.
*   (the deck it replaces had graphite 45.2%, coolant 9.2%, Zr 37.6%)
*----
LINKED_LIST LIBRARY LIBSS GEOSS GEOFL TRKSS TRK SYS FLUX
            EDIHOM EDIMIX SPHED MACMIX ;
SEQ_BINARY  FTRKSS FTRK ;
MODULE      LIB: GEO: NXT: USS: ASM: FLU: EDI: SPH: GREP: DELETE:
            UTL: ABORT: END: ;
PROCEDURE   assertS RbmkLib RbmkGeo ;

REAL dca   := 0.72 ;   ! nominal coolant density, g/cm3
REAL tfuel := 900.0 ;  ! fuel temperature, K
REAL tgrap := 750.0 ;  ! graphite temperature, K (RBMK runs 500-700 C)
REAL tcool := 573.0 ;  ! coolant and structure temperature, K
REAL kinf ;
REAL v1 v2 v3 v4 v5 v6 v7 v8 v9 vtot fgra fcool ffuel fzr fgas ;

*==============================================================
*  MICROSCOPIC LIBRARY
*  All compositions live in rbmk_proc/RbmkLib.c2m, shared with the A5 branch
*  deck so the two cannot disagree about what a mixture contains.
*==============================================================
LIBRARY := RbmkLib :: <<dca>> <<tfuel>> <<tgrap>> <<tcool>> ;

*==============================================================
*  GEOMETRY -- coarse, for self-shielding
*==============================================================
*  Both geometries come from rbmk_proc/RbmkGeo.c2m, the single source of
*  truth for the cell -- see its header for every dimension and source.
GEOSS GEOFL := RbmkGeo ;

*==============================================================
*  SELF-SHIELDING  --  absent from every previous RBMK deck, so all
*  resonance absorption up to now was at infinite dilution
*==============================================================
TRKSS FTRKSS := NXT: GEOSS ::
  EDIT 0 TITLE 'RBMK-A3-SS' ALLG BATCH 100 TISO 8 15.0 ;

LIBSS := USS: LIBRARY TRKSS FTRKSS :: EDIT 1 PASS 2 GRMIN 18 ;

*==============================================================
*  TRANSPORT
*==============================================================
TRK FTRK := NXT: GEOFL ::
  EDIT 0 TITLE 'RBMK-A3-FLUX' ALLG BATCH 100 TISO 15 30.0 ;

SYS  := ASM: LIBSS TRK FTRK :: EDIT 1 ;
FLUX := FLU: LIBSS TRK SYS :: TYPE K EXTE 1.0E-6 ;

GREP: FLUX :: GETVAL 'K-INFINITY' 1 >>kinf<< ;
ECHO "RBMK-A3 k-infinity =" kinf ;

*==============================================================
*  EDITIONS
*   EDIMIX -- per-mixture, feeds SPH and the volume check
*   EDIHOM -- fully homogenized 2-group macrolib for DONJON
*==============================================================
EDIMIX := EDI: LIBSS TRK FLUX GEOFL SYS ::
  EDIT 2 MICR ALL MERG MIX  COND 0.625 SAVE ON MIXED ;

EDIHOM := EDI: LIBSS TRK FLUX GEOFL SYS ::
  EDIT 2 MICR ALL MERG COMP COND 0.625 SAVE ON HOMOG ;

*  SPH applies to the PER-MIXTURE edition only.  Tested 2026-09-22:
*    SPH: EDIHOM ...  ->  SPHDRV: INVALID NUMBER OF MACRO-REGIONS (9 1)
*  SPH needs one homogenized region per tracking macro-region, so it cannot
*  be applied to a full-cell (MERG COMP) homogenization at all.  For the
*  DONJON model -- one node per channel -- EDIHOM is used directly and needs
*  no SPH: flux-volume weighting with reflective boundaries already preserves
*  k-infinity exactly.  SPH is needed at the CORE level instead, for the
*  graphite reflector and for control-rod cells.  That reframes task A4.
*
*  Kept here because it exercises the SEQ_BINARY tracking file that the
*  original "SPH is incompatible with NXT" blocker was really about, and
*  because a multi-region channel model would need these factors.
SPHED := SPH: EDIMIX TRK FTRK :: EDIT 2 ;

*==============================================================
*  VOLUME-FRACTION GUARDRAIL
*
*  This is the check that was missing.  The deck this replaces was a CANDU-6
*  bundle (graphite 45.2%, zirconium 37.6%) and nothing caught it -- the error
*  only surfaced when the void coefficient came out at -621 pcm/%void, six
*  branch calculations later.  A lattice deck that does not verify what it
*  actually built cannot be trusted.
*
*  2026-09-24: the pressure tube is no longer ambiguous (see [D] above), so
*  the coolant band no longer has to straddle the 88 vs 92 mm choice.  It is
*  tightened from 3.0-4.5 to 3.4-4.0.  Computed check: 88x4 gives 3.604%,
*  92x4 gives 4.428% (both at clad OD 13.58; the 4.437 quoted here before was
*  an arithmetic slip for 4.477), so the wrong tube is rejected.  Other bands unchanged --
*  they exist to reject a whole wrong reactor type, not to pin a dimension.
*==============================================================
MACMIX := EDIMIX :: STEP UP MIXED ;
GREP: MACMIX :: GETVAL 'MIXTURESVOL' 1 >>v1<< ;
GREP: MACMIX :: GETVAL 'MIXTURESVOL' 2 >>v2<< ;
GREP: MACMIX :: GETVAL 'MIXTURESVOL' 3 >>v3<< ;
GREP: MACMIX :: GETVAL 'MIXTURESVOL' 4 >>v4<< ;
GREP: MACMIX :: GETVAL 'MIXTURESVOL' 5 >>v5<< ;
GREP: MACMIX :: GETVAL 'MIXTURESVOL' 6 >>v6<< ;
GREP: MACMIX :: GETVAL 'MIXTURESVOL' 7 >>v7<< ;
GREP: MACMIX :: GETVAL 'MIXTURESVOL' 8 >>v8<< ;
GREP: MACMIX :: GETVAL 'MIXTURESVOL' 9 >>v9<< ;

EVALUATE vtot  := v1 v2 + v3 + v4 + v5 + v6 + v7 + v8 + v9 + ;
EVALUATE fgra  := v4 v5 + vtot / 100.0 * ;
EVALUATE fcool := v1 vtot / 100.0 * ;
EVALUATE ffuel := v6 v7 + vtot / 100.0 * ;
EVALUATE fzr   := v2 v8 + v9 + vtot / 100.0 * ;
EVALUATE fgas  := v3 vtot / 100.0 * ;

ECHO "-----------------------------------------------------" ;
ECHO "RBMK-A3 cell area cm2 :" vtot "   (expect 625.0)" ;
ECHO "  graphite  %          :" fgra  "   (expect 89.59)" ;
ECHO "  coolant   %          :" fcool "   (expect  3.60)" ;
ECHO "  fuel      %          :" ffuel "   (expect  2.90)" ;
ECHO "  zirconium %          :" fzr   "   (expect  3.03)" ;
ECHO "  gas       %          :" fgas  "   (expect  0.87)" ;
ECHO "  k-infinity           :" kinf ;
ECHO "-----------------------------------------------------" ;

IF vtot 624.0 < THEN
  ECHO "FAIL: cell area is not 25 x 25 cm" ; ABORT: ; ENDIF ;
IF vtot 626.0 > THEN
  ECHO "FAIL: cell area is not 25 x 25 cm" ; ABORT: ; ENDIF ;
IF fgra 88.0 < THEN
  ECHO "FAIL: graphite fraction too low -- this is not an RBMK cell" ;
  ABORT: ; ENDIF ;
IF fgra 91.0 > THEN
  ECHO "FAIL: graphite fraction too high -- channel is missing" ;
  ABORT: ; ENDIF ;
IF fcool 3.4 < THEN
  ECHO "FAIL: too little coolant" ; ABORT: ; ENDIF ;
IF fcool 4.0 > THEN
  ECHO "FAIL: too much coolant -- wrong pressure tube (92x4?) or wrong type" ;
  ABORT: ; ENDIF ;
IF ffuel 2.5 < THEN
  ECHO "FAIL: too little fuel" ; ABORT: ; ENDIF ;
IF ffuel 3.3 > THEN
  ECHO "FAIL: too much fuel -- wrong number of pins?" ; ABORT: ; ENDIF ;
IF fzr 3.5 > THEN
  ECHO "FAIL: too much zirconium -- is there a calandria tube in here?" ;
  ABORT: ; ENDIF ;
ECHO "volume-fraction guardrail PASSED" ;

END: ;
QUIT "LIST" .
